Save93 / Whiterun exterior / stock VM stage attribution of late DynDOLOD GetWorldSpace publication / 2026-11-09

Setup and evidence
- Skyrim AE 1.6.1170.0, same Save93 and disposable profile as the preceding native drain experiment. SSE Display Tweaks 0.5.16, gameplay cap 42 FPS, dynamic Papyrus budget, frame generation off only in the disposable profile. One Save93 load and four Bannered Mare to WhiterunWorld returns, 32 Utility.Wait(0.01) responses per trial.
- Preserve native drain, retry, and tasklet behavior. Observe the stock drain 104857, suspended retry 104858 and subsequent stock stages 104859 and 104860. Stage timestamps are on the update thread. Correlate the actual delayed enqueue bracket, native FIFO pop, and preceding depth-1 return on the same stack. Enqueue inside the original VMProcess additionally records its start tick from thread-local same-stack context. A worker event inside a stage's wall-clock interval alone would not prove it was called by the stage.
- At the end of 104860, record the current FIFO head and overflow flag while holding the stock queue lock. Count a same-render-frame head candidate only if publication finished by the stage end, the target is the actual call-message head with no overflow and remains the first pop of the next drain. This is a local observation of FIFO order. The hook is inside the stock VM update and does not measure the outer update exit or the completion of all tasklet jobs.
- The preliminary process was closed before Save93 load while adding exact VMProcess context. No trials from that process are included. Final observation DLL SHA256 4E59374D325E183D17203F7F0F547930BFDA4FD8994FE64B98CE4E5849B8FF10.
- APBGameplayTrace built, budget policy checks passed, synthetic timing checks covered stage boundaries, cross-thread tasklet context, incomplete cycles, frame mismatch, head rejection and next-pop order. Runtime installation passed the exact call/prologue verification.
- Raw capture: build/gameplay-trace/cell-42-getworldspace-stage-observe-full.

