Interpretation
- 1490 complete cycles between recorded native drains. Of 88 GetWorldSpace calls overlapping the final DynDOLOD stack's lock wait, 77 registered after the earlier drain's last decision. 68 had missed an empty drain and nine published after an expired drain. Eleven were already pending at a budget stop.
- For the 77 later registrations, the preceding return was GetAt in 75 and GetSize in two. It completed on the drain/update thread inside the preceding native drain in 68 cases and during 104858 in nine. The next VMProcess began after that return, and after 104860, in all 77. Of their enqueues, 58 ran on a different thread from the stock drain, 19 on the same thread.
- No target from the 77 late publications was already in the FIFO at the end of 104860, so the same-frame head gate had zero candidates at that site. This says nothing about a later, valid job-completion boundary. A future placement needs a verified job completion boundary, original FIFO and phase ordering, and a supported native execution context.
- The four windows completed and PresentMon exited 0. The response and render figures are stock observation metrics. No accelerated condition was run.

